{
  "title": "break, continue, and loop else",
  "summary": "Leave early, skip ahead, and know when nothing was found.",
  "minutes": 10,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "break and continue",
      "body": [
        "Same as C#: `break` leaves the loop, `continue` skips to the next pass.",
        "",
        "```python",
        "for n in range(1, 10):",
        "    if n % 2 == 0:",
        "        continue      # skip even numbers",
        "    if n > 7:",
        "        break         # stop altogether",
        "    print(n)          # 1 3 5 7",
        "```",
        "",
        "For a loop that runs \"until something happens\", write `while True:` and `break` out."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "What does this print?",
      "code": [
        "for ch in \"programming\":",
        "    if ch == \"g\":",
        "        break",
        "    if ch in \"aeiou\":",
        "        continue",
        "    print(ch, end=\"\")",
        "print()"
      ],
      "answer": "pr",
      "explain": "Vowels are skipped with `continue`, and the loop stops at the first `g`. Before it come `p`, `r`, `o`: the `o` is skipped."
    },
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "for ... else",
      "body": [
        "Python loops can have an `else` block. It runs only if the loop finished **without** `break`:",
        "",
        "```python",
        "for n in numbers:",
        "    if n < 0:",
        "        print(\"found a negative:\", n)",
        "        break",
        "else:",
        "    print(\"no negatives\")",
        "```",
        "",
        "Read the `else` as \"no break\". It replaces C#'s `bool found = false;` flag pattern."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "When does the `else` block of a `for` loop run?",
      "options": [
        "When the loop ends without hitting `break`",
        "When the loop body never runs, only",
        "When the condition is false on the first pass",
        "When an exception is raised in the loop"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "explain": "It runs when the loop runs out of items normally, including when there were no items. A `break` skips it."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "What does this print?",
      "code": [
        "for n in [4, 6, 9, 10]:",
        "    if n % 2:",
        "        print(\"odd:\", n)",
        "        break",
        "else:",
        "    print(\"all even\")",
        "for n in [2, 8]:",
        "    if n % 2:",
        "        break",
        "else:",
        "    print(\"all even\")"
      ],
      "answer": [
        "odd: 9",
        "all even"
      ],
      "explain": "The first loop breaks at 9, so its `else` is skipped. The second finishes normally."
    },
    {
      "type": "order",
      "prompt": "Arrange the lines into a prime test for `n` that prints `prime` or `composite`.",
      "lines": [
        "n = 29",
        "for d in range(2, n):",
        "    if n % d == 0:",
        "        print(\"composite\")",
        "        break",
        "else:",
        "    print(\"prime\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sort",
      "prompt": "Where does each statement send the program next?",
      "buckets": [
        "Next pass of the loop",
        "Out of the loop"
      ],
      "items": [
        [
          "`continue`",
          0
        ],
        [
          "`break`",
          1
        ],
        [
          "reaching the end of the body",
          0
        ],
        [
          "`for` running out of items",
          1
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Guess the number",
      "prompt": "The secret number is `42`. Read guesses, one per line. After each, print `higher`, `lower`, or `correct in N` (N = guesses so far) and stop. If a line is `quit`, print `gave up` and stop.",
      "starter": "SECRET = 42\n",
      "solution": [
        "SECRET = 42",
        "tries = 0",
        "while True:",
        "    line = input()",
        "    if line == \"quit\":",
        "        print(\"gave up\")",
        "        break",
        "    tries += 1",
        "    guess = int(line)",
        "    if guess < SECRET:",
        "        print(\"higher\")",
        "    elif guess > SECRET:",
        "        print(\"lower\")",
        "    else:",
        "        print(f\"correct in {tries}\")",
        "        break"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "name": "three guesses",
          "stdin": "50\n25\n42\n",
          "expect": [
            "lower",
            "higher",
            "correct in 3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "first try",
          "stdin": "42\n",
          "expect": "correct in 1"
        },
        {
          "name": "gives up",
          "stdin": "10\nquit\n",
          "expect": [
            "higher",
            "gave up"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`while True:` with `break` when correct or on `quit`.",
        "Check for `quit` before converting with `int`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "First repeated word",
      "prompt": "Read one line of words. Print the first word that appears a second time (comparing in lowercase), as `repeat: word`. If no word repeats, print `all unique`. Use a `for ... else`.",
      "starter": "words = input().lower().split()\n",
      "solution": [
        "words = input().lower().split()",
        "seen = []",
        "for w in words:",
        "    if w in seen:",
        "        print(f\"repeat: {w}\")",
        "        break",
        "    seen.append(w)",
        "else:",
        "    print(\"all unique\")"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "name": "repeats",
          "stdin": "The cat saw the dog\n",
          "expect": "repeat: the"
        },
        {
          "name": "unique",
          "stdin": "one two three\n",
          "expect": "all unique"
        },
        {
          "name": "later repeat",
          "stdin": "a b c b a\n",
          "expect": "repeat: b"
        }
      ],
      "require": [
        {
          "pattern": "\\belse\\s*:",
          "message": "Uses a loop else"
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "Keep a list `seen` and `append` each word after checking `in seen`.",
        "Put `else:` level with `for`, not with `if`."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
